result.costModel:
METHOD
- Warm wall ms on this 4-core box. Source: trcycles runs, executions > 6, instrumented copy of B (88 in-step marks).
- 7 cities: s10 128² (3.5k road nodes); vet_s7_y21 (10.9k); bot256 (13.8k); vet_s7_y43 (13.8k); dense1m (23.1k); stress1m and generated stress 256 (36.0k, 19.5k buildings, 14k origins).
- One designated driver per in-step part; one point per city (the median); least squares ms = a + b·x, or b0·x through the origin when the intercept is ≈ 0 or negative.
- To get the interleaved headless schedule (colder caches), multiply by about 1.2: warm-headless / trcycles medians are 0.8-1.5 (median 1.2) at dense1m and 0.75-1.1 (median 0.95) at bot256.

UNITS: n = road nodes, C = cells, B = buildings (scan snapshot), oN = origins, jN/jB = job sites, qN = clusters, S = stops, T = transit nodes, nc = candidates, fN = freight sources, k = chunk work units. Coefficients are ms per 1000 units.

PER-UNIT COEFFICIENTS (max |rel. err| over the 7 cities in brackets)
Searches:
- Dial road search: 0.066/1k settled (b0) [29%], or −0.21 + 0.074/1k. Slightly superlinear: 0.05/1k at 14k nodes, 0.07/1k at 36k.
- transit search: 0.071/1k (b0) [50%], or −0.23 + 0.079/1k [best at T ≥ 10k].
- accumulate 0.0054/1k; commit 0.0052/1k.
- P&R K-label search (K = 5): 0.16-0.22/1k states; overflow (K = 4, lazy): 0.17/1k; refreshAlt 0.014-0.018/1k states.
Prep and matching:
- building scan 0.17/1k B (b0) [27%] (a = 0.47, b = 0.143);
- node times + ramps + fills 0.014/1k n [41%];
- origin init 0.012/1k oN; clusters 0.046/1k jN [13%]; jNoise + capacities 0.014/1k jN; regional ≈ 0.02 + 0.01/1k jN;
- candidates 0.017/1k oN [16%]; keys 0.010/1k nc [20%]; radix sort 0.027/1k nc [14%]; accept 0.057/1k nc [27%]; nextRound 0.0024/1k oN;
- pool main 0.08/1k nc [25%]; pool U/O/avg ≈ 0.012/1k oN + 0.01/1k qN;
- commute.end parts: prices 0.035/1k qN, distribution 0.015/1k jN, snapReach 0.024/1k oN, transit accumulate 0.0085/1k T, transit flows 0.0085/1k T, cut 0.0024/1k oN, per-origin 0.016/1k oN, by-mode 0.010/1k oN.
Transit and stops:
- transit2 per origin: 0.07 + 0.0043·ρ µs, ρ = stops per 1000 cells (dense1m 0.27 µs; ±40% elsewhere);
- stop attach 0.10/1k S; waits 0.05/1k S; transfers 0.17-0.19/1k S (density-dependent); stop loads in final 0.23/1k S; collectStops 0.036/1k B.
Post-search parts:
- inbound desire + apply 0.03/1k jB; shop origins 0.032/1k oN [10%]; freight sources 0.049/1k fN; truck times 0.0031/1k n.
Cell and node passes:
- box filter 0.0055/1k C each (boxD 8%, boxS 13%); baseSupply 0.0042/1k C; parkingFromBoxes 0.009/1k C; demand footprints 0.1/1k jB; whole parking 0.0305/1k C [22%];
- MSA blend 0.0036/1k n, ramp 0.0041/1k n, write 0.0063/1k n; layer fills 0.0006/1k C;
- cached volume adds 0.0085/1k n (inbound) and 0.0026/1k n (shop, freight).
Final2 and graph build:
- final2: origins 0.19/1k oN [19%] (a ≈ −0.09); job sites 0.145/1k jB; events ≈ 0.04/1k oN (depends on flag flips: 0.03-0.6 ms); saveTransport 0.017/1k n (+ C on recompute cycles); routes 0.0136/1k oN;
- graph build: road ≈ 0.008/1k C + 0.06/1k n; rail and subway GridGraph ≈ 0.012/1k C each (one closure call per cell); attach refresh when dirty 0.3-1.2 ms at 256².

STEP FORMULAS
The formulas for the proposed sub-steps are written next to each proposal (est = constant 0.03-0.05 + the part terms of that sub-step). Validation of the part sums against today's steps, warm, per city:
- prep 0.6+0.20·B/1k: b0 0.24/1k B [26%];
- final2: b0 0.339/1k oN [28%];
- roundMatch: b0 0.166/1k nc [11%];
- parking 0.0305/1k C [22%];
- inbound 0.095/1k n [22%]; shop 0.093/1k n [26%]; freight 0.078/1k n [32%];
- roundSearch 0.066/1k n [29%];
- commute.pool 0.116/1k oN [19%]; commute.end 0.109/1k oN [36%];
- transit −0.16 + 0.092/1k T;
- prepTransit and final need their stops terms: single-driver fits err 49-60%.
- With these the median |error| of the step estimates over the 7 cities is about 10-20%, inside ±30%.
Where a single size driver is weak (transit2, transfers, transit seeds, final2 events), charge per unit of a WORK COUNTER from the previous cycle: (origin, attach-node) pairs, transfer pairs, seeds pushed, flags flipped. This is deterministic (state, not clock) and tracks density. Fall back to the size formula on the first cycle after a load.

